ID: vr-62
Title: Reduce real-chat animated reply preparation latency

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: Post-M1 measured responsiveness
Dependencies: vr-61

Purpose:
  Address measured delay before an uncached animated reply speaks, without
  silently substituting voice-only output or degrading the requested face.

Tasks:
  Attribute warm synthesis, neutral/emotional inference, packing/delivery and
    player preparation with bounded phase timings on short synthetic replies.
  Compare matching workloads with fixed source/settings and report contention.
  Implement only source-traced bottleneck fixes, retaining latest-only ownership.
  Compare final audio/motion, cancellation and repeated/novel-text latency.

Acceptance criteria:
  Reproduce the delay and identify its dominant phase before choosing a fix.
  Preserve voice, expressions, full-head cursor behavior and requested quality.
  No new cloud service, retained transcripts, unbounded cache or global tuning.
  Report matched latency distributions and retained failures, not an SLA inferred
    from one interactive sample or a cache hit on repeated benchmark text.

Completion evidence:
  .local\qualification\live-use-01\receipt.json: real owned warm Claire/Hazel
    summary, both caches false, playback start 21.412s and total 30.220s.
    Generating-labelled intervals average 11.73% of 16-logical-CPU machine;
    whole-machine load 52.31%, so this is not isolated causal attribution.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Opened from real session use at the owner's request. Investigation
    and optimization are planned, not implemented or measured improvements.
